{"merge_recommendation":"REQUEST_CHANGES","highest_risk":"P2","investigated_safe":["backend/src/common/error-codes/modules/store-membership.ts","backend/src/modules/audit-log/enums/audit-action.enum.ts","backend/src/modules/membership/membership.controller.ts (split, splitPreview, activeSplit)","backend/src/modules/membership/membership.module.ts","backend/src/modules/membership/dto/membership-split.dto.ts","backend/src/modules/store-member/services/store-member.serializer.ts","frontend/src/@core/components/api-url/live/membership.js","frontend/src/@core/components/api-url/store.js","frontend/src/constants/errorCode/store-membership.js","frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MemberDetailTabs.js","backend/test/e2e/membership-split.e2e-spec.ts","frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/__tests__/MembershipOrderRow.test.js","frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipSplitDialog.test.js"],"assumptions":["The service layer guarantees that `idempotency_key` and `child_membership_ids` are always provided on INSERT.","StoreWriteGuard correctly enforces store-level write permissions for all new endpoints.","MembershipSplitStatus enum values are used consistently across the codebase.","Backend split endpoints (/memberships/splits/active, preview, split, revert) are implemented, authorized, and return expected shapes (out of scope for this PR group).","MembershipOrderRow accepts an optional onSplit prop and safely handles undefined values before invocation.","Backend split service (membership-split.service.ts) may allow splitting memberships with statuses other than ACTIVE (e.g. HELD, EXPIRED); the frontend hardcodes ms.status === 'ACTIVE' as the only visible condition.","The backend has no separate limit on split recipients; MAX_RECIPIENTS = 9 is a frontend-only constant that may diverge from backend constraints.","The preview API accepts any selected memberIds list without validation; no client-side guard exists before the API call.","MembershipLiveCard and MembershipSplitNotice are new or updated components that correctly implement the expected props (onSplit, split, busy, onRevert) as wired in MembershipTab.js.","Backend services and controllers for membership-split are assumed correct based on the diff provided.","Migrations 1794000000440 and 1794000000441 are assumed to be correctly implemented and non-colliding with existing migrations.","Local review incomplete: 1 group(s) failed (backend/src/modules/membership/services/membership-split.helpers.ts, backend/src/modules/membership/services/membership-split.service.ts)"],"findings":[{"severity":"P1","file":"backend/src/modules/membership/services/membership-split.service.ts","line":115,"side":"RIGHT","title":"revert() fails on retry due to unhandled unique constraint violation","failure_scenario":"A client retries a split revert with the same idempotency key. The unique constraint UQ_membership_split_store_idempotency is violated, throwing a 500 error instead of returning the prior result.","root_cause":"splitService.confirm() catches unique constraint errors and replays the prior split. splitService.revert() does not catch unique constraint errors, so retries with the same key fail with a database error.","evidence":"backend/src/modules/membership/services/membership-split.service.ts:115: `return this.dataSource.transaction(async (manager) => { ... revertSplit(...) });` lacks unique constraint handling.","recommended_fix":"Wrap the transaction in a try/catch, check for unique constraint violations, and if found, look up the prior split by idempotencyKey and return its result (similar to confirm()).","recommended_test":"Add an e2e test for splitRevert that retries with the same idempotency key and verifies it returns 200 with the prior split data."},{"severity":"P1","file":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipRowActions.js","line":92,"side":"RIGHT","title":"Split button only visible for ACTIVE memberships; backend may support splitting other statuses","failure_scenario":"A membership in HELD, EXPIRED, or other non-ACTIVE status can be split by the backend but the UI never shows the split button. The operator cannot discover this capability, creating a silent gap between available and exposed functionality.","root_cause":"Line 92 hardcodes `ms.status === 'ACTIVE'` as the visibility condition for the split button. The backend split logic (membership-split.service.ts) may not restrict to ACTIVE status, so valid splits exist that the UI never exposes.","evidence":"MembershipRowActions.js:92-97: `{onSplit && ms.status === 'ACTIVE' && !readOnly ? (
      <RowButton
        label={t('store.members.detail.memberships.split.action')}
        onClick={() => onSplit(ms)}
      />
    ) : null}`","recommended_fix":"Remove or relax the `ms.status === 'ACTIVE'` condition. The split button should be visible whenever `onSplit` is provided and the row is not read-only, matching the backend's actual allowed statuses.","recommended_test":"Integration test: open split dialog for a membership with status 'HELD' and 'EXPIRED'; verify the split button is rendered (or document why it should not be). Cross-check backend membership-split.service.ts allowed statuses."},{"severity":"P1","file":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipSplitDialog.js","line":32,"side":"RIGHT","title":"selected state not reset on dialog close; stale selections persist across open/close cycles","failure_scenario":"User opens split dialog, selects members, closes dialog (without confirming). User reopens dialog — previously selected members remain selected, confusing the operator and potentially submitting an unintended split.","root_cause":"Line 32-35: `useEffect` clears `selected` only when `!open` (dialog closing), but does NOT reset it when `open` transitions from false to true (dialog opening). The state persists across the lifecycle. The useEffect at line 33-35 only fires on `open` becoming false, not on it becoming true.","evidence":"MembershipSplitDialog.js:32-35: `const [selected, setSelected] = useState([])
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!open) setSelected([])
  }, [open])`","recommended_fix":"Add a second useEffect that resets `selected([])` when `open` becomes true, or initialize `selected` from the `preview` prop if one exists. Example: `useEffect(() => { if (open) setSelected([]) }, [open])` — or better, clear on open AND reset to preview selections if preview is provided.","recommended_test":"Unit test: open dialog, select members, close, reopen — verify `selected` is empty (or matches preview). E2E: select members → close dialog → reopen → verify no pre-selected members."},{"severity":"P1","file":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipSplitDialog.js","line":67,"side":"RIGHT","title":"onSelectionChange called synchronously inside state updater triggers preview API during render","failure_scenario":"Rapidly toggling multiple candidates fires multiple preview API calls in quick succession. The latest API response may be stale relative to the current selection, causing the preview to show incorrect allocation data. No cancellation or debouncing exists.","root_cause":"Line 67: `onSelectionChange?.({ memberIds: next })` is called synchronously inside the `setSelected` updater. This triggers a preview API call every time the user clicks a candidate, with no debounce, cancellation, or stale-response handling. Rapid clicks produce overlapping requests.","evidence":"MembershipSplitDialog.js:58-69: `const toggle = (id) => {
    if (busy) return
    setSelected((previous) => {
      if (!previous.includes(id) && previous.length >= MAX_RECIPIENTS) {
        return previous
      }
      const next = previous.includes(id)
        ? previous.filter((value) => value !== id)
        : [...previous, id]
      onSelectionChange?.({ memberIds: next })
      return next
    })
  }`","recommended_fix":"Move `onSelectionChange` outside the state updater, or use a ref + useEffect pattern to trigger the preview after the state update is flushed. Add debounce (e.g. 300ms) or request cancellation (AbortController) to prevent overlapping/stale preview calls.","recommended_test":"E2E: rapidly toggle 5+ candidates; verify that the preview shows data matching the final selection, not an intermediate one. Test with slow network to observe race conditions."},{"severity":"P1","file":"frontend/src/pages/store/members/[id].js","line":786,"side":"RIGHT","title":"Idempotency key lost on split-revert retry","failure_scenario":"Split revert request fails (e.g., network timeout or 5xx). The confirmation dialog remains open. If the operator clicks submit again, a new idempotency key is generated because the splitRevertConfirm state object was never updated with the key created during the first attempt. The backend receives a different key, breaking idempotency and risking duplicate reversions or rejected retries.","root_cause":"runSplitRevert updates the lastSplit state with the newly generated key but does not update the splitRevertConfirm state. The dialog's onSuccess handler reads from splitRevertConfirm, so retries bypass the stored key.","evidence":"frontend/src/pages/store/members/[id].js:786-791: const action = splitRevertConfirm\n    const idempotencyKey = action.revertKey || newTransferIdempotencyKey()\n    setSplitRevertBusy(true)\n    setLastSplit((previous) => previous ? { ...previous, revertKey: idempotencyKey } : previous)","recommended_fix":"Update splitRevertConfirm state with the new key alongside lastSplit (e.g., setSplitRevertConfirm((prev) => (prev ? { ...prev, revertKey: idempotencyKey } : prev))), matching the pattern already used correctly in runTransfer.","recommended_test":"Add a unit test for runSplitRevert that mocks a failing API call, verifies the state is updated with a new idempotency key, and asserts that a subsequent submit call uses the exact same key."},{"severity":"P2","file":"backend/src/migrations/1794000000440-CreateMembershipSplit.ts","line":25,"side":"RIGHT","title":"Unique index on nullable `idempotency_key` permits duplicate NULLs","failure_scenario":"If the service omits `idempotency_key`, MySQL allows multiple rows with NULL, bypassing idempotency protection and creating duplicate splits.","root_cause":"MySQL UNIQUE indexes allow multiple NULL values by default. The column is defined as `VARCHAR(128) NULL` but participates in a UNIQUE constraint.","evidence":"backend/src/migrations/1794000000440-CreateMembershipSplit.ts:25: UNIQUE KEY `UQ_membership_split_store_idempotency` (`store_id`, `idempotency_key`)","recommended_fix":"Define `idempotency_key` as `NOT NULL` and ensure the service always provides one, or use a generated column/index that handles NULLs explicitly.","recommended_test":"Insert two rows with NULL `idempotency_key` and verify the second insert fails with a duplicate key error."},{"severity":"P2","file":"backend/src/migrations/1794000000440-CreateMembershipSplit.ts","line":13,"side":"RIGHT","title":"`child_membership_ids` JSON column lacks default value","failure_scenario":"An INSERT statement that omits `child_membership_ids` will fail with a SQL error, crashing the split confirmation transaction.","root_cause":"The column is defined as `JSON NOT NULL` without a default value. TypeORM may skip writing the column if it matches the entity's default `[]`, causing a mismatch between ORM behavior and strict SQL constraints.","evidence":"backend/src/migrations/1794000000440-CreateMembershipSplit.ts:13: `child_membership_ids` JSON NOT NULL,","recommended_fix":"Add a default value (e.g., `JSON '[]'`) or ensure the service explicitly passes it on every insert.","recommended_test":"Insert a row omitting `child_membership_ids` and verify it fails gracefully or succeeds with the default."},{"severity":"P2","file":"backend/src/modules/membership/membership.controller.ts","line":217,"side":"RIGHT","title":"splitRevert() inconsistent idempotency handling","failure_scenario":"A frontend sends an idempotency header but no body key for a revert. The controller passes undefined to the service, bypassing header/body validation and allowing non-idempotent retries with different keys.","root_cause":"splitRevert() does not call assertHeaderMatchesBodyKey() and does not fallback to the header key, unlike split().","evidence":"backend/src/modules/membership/membership.controller.ts:217: `const result = await this.splitService.revert({ ... idempotencyKey: dto.idempotencyKey, ... }, user.id);`","recommended_fix":"Add `assertHeaderMatchesBodyKey(headerKey, dto.idempotencyKey);` and change the service call to `idempotencyKey: dto.idempotencyKey ?? headerKey`.","recommended_test":"Add an e2e test for splitRevert with header-only key and verify it behaves consistently with split()."},{"severity":"P2","file":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipLiveCard.js","line":87,"side":"RIGHT","title":"Missing guard for optional onSplit prop propagation","failure_scenario":"MembershipLiveCard receives onSplit as undefined from a parent that does not support splitting. It passes undefined to MembershipOrderRow, which may invoke it directly, causing a runtime TypeError.","root_cause":"MembershipLiveCard destructures onSplit from props and passes it to MembershipOrderRow without checking for existence or providing a no-op fallback.","evidence":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipLiveCard.js:87 passes onSplit={onSplit} to MembershipOrderRow. MembershipOrderRow definition was not in the provided snapshot.","recommended_fix":"Add a guard or default no-op function: onSplit={onSplit ?? (() => {})} or verify MembershipOrderRow handles undefined gracefully.","recommended_test":"Unit test MembershipLiveCard rendering with onSplit=undefined and verify no console error or crash when MembershipOrderRow attempts to call it."},{"severity":"P2","file":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipSplitDialog.js","line":14,"side":"RIGHT","title":"MAX_RECIPIENTS hardcoded to 9 with no backend validation or configuration","failure_scenario":"If the backend allows more than 9 split recipients, the UI silently prevents valid operations. If the backend limit is lower, the UI allows selections that will be rejected by the backend with a confusing error.","root_cause":"Line 14: `const MAX_RECIPIENTS = 9` is a magic number with no connection to backend constraints. It is not configurable, not documented, and not validated against the backend.","evidence":"MembershipSplitDialog.js:14: `const MAX_RECIPIENTS = 9`","recommended_fix":"Either (a) make MAX_RECIPIENTS a configurable prop, or (b) fetch the limit from the backend preview endpoint, or (c) document the hardcoded value and ensure the backend enforces the same limit.","recommended_test":"Test with 9 and 10 recipients; verify backend behavior matches the UI limit. Document the constraint in code comments."},{"severity":"P2","file":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipSplitCandidates.js","line":36,"side":"RIGHT","title":"selected.includes(member.id) does not validate member.id type; numeric IDs may fail equality check","failure_scenario":"If `member.id` is a number and `selected` contains strings (or vice versa), `selected.includes(member.id)` returns false, causing the checkbox to show the wrong checked state and the item to appear unselected.","root_cause":"Line 36: `selected.includes(member.id)` performs strict equality. The `selected` state in MembershipSplitDialog is populated with string IDs (line 51: `String(id)`), but `member.id` from the candidates list may be a number. No type coercion is applied.","evidence":"MembershipSplitCandidates.js:36: `selected={selected.includes(member.id)}`","recommended_fix":"Use `String(member.id)` in the includes check: `selected.includes(String(member.id))`. Ensure consistency between how IDs are stored and compared.","recommended_test":"Unit test: candidate with numeric ID vs selected array containing string IDs; verify checkbox reflects correct state."},{"severity":"P2","file":"frontend/public/locales/en/pages/store/members.json","line":493,"side":"RIGHT","title":"Typo in English locale 'familys'","failure_scenario":"User sees 'Issue with familys' instead of 'Issue with families'.","root_cause":"Typo in the new i18n keys for the 'family' split feature.","evidence":""title": "Issue with familys", "toggle": "Issue with familys"","recommended_fix":"Correct 'familys' to 'families'.","recommended_test":"Verify English locale renders correctly."},{"severity":"P2","file":"frontend/public/locales/kr/pages/store/members.json","line":506,"side":"RIGHT","title":"Grammar error in Korean locale '가족를'","failure_scenario":"User sees grammatically incorrect Korean text.","root_cause":"Typo in the new i18n keys for the 'family' split feature.","evidence":""count": "가족를 한 명 이상 추가해 주세요"","recommended_fix":"Correct '가족를' to '가족을'.","recommended_test":"Verify Korean locale renders correctly."},{"severity":"P2","file":"frontend/src/page-lib/store/members/components/MembershipSplitDialog.js","line":40,"side":"RIGHT","title":"Missing `locale` prop passed to `MembershipSplitDialog`","failure_scenario":"Date/currency formatting falls back to default (likely en-US), breaking localization.","root_cause":"`locale` is extracted in `MembershipSplitDialog` but never passed by its caller `MembershipOrderRow`.","evidence":"<MembershipSplitDialog ... t={t} />","recommended_fix":"Pass `locale={locale}` from `MembershipOrderRow` to `MembershipSplitDialog`.","recommended_test":"Add a test verifying `locale` is passed to `MembershipSplitDialog`."}],"coverage":[{"file":"backend/src/common/error-codes/modules/store-membership.ts","status":"cleared","reason":"Error code additions are declarative; reviewed full diff and snapshot for correctness."},{"file":"backend/src/migrations/17940